Switch: report and end the boot pipeline warm-up (aurora_switch_get_precompile/_stop_precompile)

At start Aurora queues every pipeline its cache knows (the player's pipeline_cache.db, seeded from
the bundled initial_pipeline_cache.db next to the NRO) on the compile thread's background queue, in
order of first use, and builds them all. On the Switch each build holds the single GL context for
0.1-0.4 s (Mesa 20.1 compiles and links every program from source; it has no program binaries), so
the render worker draws about one frame per build: with 271 known pipelines the boot logos ran at
7 frames/s for 29 s. A warm-up that keeps going into gameplay is a stutter per pipeline.

This patch counts the warm-up (pipelines queued, built - by it or first for a draw -, pending,
dropped, compile thread time) for the harness's "[cos] precompile" lines, and adds
aurora_switch_stop_precompile: the warm-up entries no draw has asked for leave the queue (a draw
queues them again as usual), a later render target layout change queues no new warm-up, and the
Dawn cache prune that follows a completed warm-up is skipped (it would delete the cache entries
of every dropped pipeline). Nothing changes unless the harness calls it.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

diff --git a/include/aurora/switch_precompile.h b/include/aurora/switch_precompile.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d4b0eae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/aurora/switch_precompile.h
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+#pragma once
+
+/* Switch build (switch/native/aurora/patches): the boot pipeline warm-up. At start Aurora queues every
+ * pipeline its pipeline cache knows (the player's pipeline_cache.db, seeded from the bundled
+ * initial_pipeline_cache.db) for its compile thread, in order of first use. This reports how far
+ * that got, and ends it: on the Switch every pipeline build holds the one GL context for 0.1-0.4 s,
+ * so warming up is only worth it while the game shows logos and menus. */
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+typedef struct {
+  uint32_t total;     /* pipelines the warm-up queued */
+  uint32_t done;      /* of those, built (by the warm-up, or first because a draw needed it) */
+  uint32_t pending;   /* still to build */
+  uint32_t dropped;   /* taken off the queue by aurora_switch_stop_precompile */
+  uint64_t compileNs; /* compile thread time spent on the built ones */
+  bool stopped;       /* aurora_switch_stop_precompile was called */
+} AuroraSwitchPrecompile;
+
+void aurora_switch_get_precompile(AuroraSwitchPrecompile* out);
+
+/* Ends the warm-up: the pipelines it has not built yet (and no draw has asked for) leave the
+ * compile queue and are built when first drawn; a later render target layout change queues none.
+ * Returns how many were dropped. */
+uint32_t aurora_switch_stop_precompile(void);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
